{"id":101,"explanation":"Do not cache get_user for the lifetime of a process: after a role is revoked, the cached user could retain stale roles. #640 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"Check the error from db.Query before calling defer rows.Close(). On an error, rows is nil, so closing it would be unsafe.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"The setTimeout call delays measure(el) until layout has settled; replacing it with queueMicrotask would measure too early.","unsure":""}
{"id":104,"explanation":"Never log the contents of the Secret<String> token. Its Debug representation is redacted and is the only permitted form for debugging output.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"RetryCount and the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json must be updated together so their retry values stay consistent.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"Before passing offset to ch.map, ensure it is divisible by pageSize. The memory mapping operation rejects offsets that are not page aligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"Keep the trailing slash on the rsync source build/: rsync then copies the directory’s contents into $DEST, rather than copying the build directory itself.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The index on events.created_at uses BRIN because the table is appended in time order; the comment says this BRIN index is 1% of the size of a btree index.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"Replace this loop, which repeatedly checks flag while waiting, with a futex based wait. The stated completion condition is that lock_acquire in src/sync/lock.c sleeps while waiting.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"Consult the failover section of the runbook, identified by doc:runbook#failover, for the reason dbo.RebuildStats runs on the secondary.","unsure":"The comment points to the reason but does not state what that reason is."}
{"id":111,"explanation":"Keep this timeout below 60 seconds because the upstream proxy terminates idle requests after 60 seconds; the value here is 30 seconds.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"Keep Widget’s destructor virtual. If it becomes non-virtual, deleting a derived object through a Widget pointer could skip the derived destructor. #915 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"Enable foreign keys before any database write on this connection. The PRAGMA setting applies separately to each connection.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"Keep Name as string[40], a ShortString, because the containing record is written directly to disk byte for byte; changing it to string would change its stored representation.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"Treat p_id as caller input and pass it through a bind variable, as the USING clause does. Concatenating that input into EXECUTE IMMEDIATE would allow SQL injection.","unsure":""}
